# Scanned / paper filings: image-only PDFs (no extractable text), large, and
# they yield nothing to the parser (parse_confidence: "none"). build.py
# re-fetches them on demand. See docs/HOUSE_DISCLOSURE_EXTRACTOR_EVAL.md §5.
2023_8220593.pdf
2024_9115596.pdf
2023_8220569.pdf
2024_9115586.pdf

# Any other large PDF (>1 MB is almost always a scanned attachment set).
*.pdf.tmp

# pipeline/financial_disclosures/build.py (Phase 1, full-scale) caches every
# downloaded filing PDF under a per-reporting-year subdirectory
# (<year>/<doc_id>.pdf) -- thousands of files across 2013-2026. Unlike the
# dozen flat fixture PDFs above (kept as committed test fixtures), the bulk
# cache is straightforwardly re-fetchable via build.py and isn't committed,
# to keep the repo from ballooning by hundreds of MB of re-derivable PDFs.
# The per-year index files (<year>FD.raw) ARE committed -- small, and they're
# the crosswalk source, not re-derivable from anything else in the repo.
20*/

